A lacuna on a mapping inside an each body, which would have to aggregate over
the list's elements like a drop's does. Not supported yet; only a
DroppedField lacuna on a drop in the body is.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	items: [...{
		title?: string
	}]
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	items: [...{
		name: string
	}]
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		items: each(v0_0.items, {
			name: orelse(item.title, "untitled")
		})
	}
	lacunas: {
		items: {
			name: [{
				type:    Placeholder
				message: "the item had no title"
			}]
		}
	}
}

BackwardLens: {
	v1_0: _
	v0_0: {
		items: each(v1_0.items, {
			title: item.name
		})
	}
}
-- out/error --
lacunas.items.name: a lacuna on a mapping inside each is not supported yet; a DroppedField lacuna on a drop refines the drop's:
    1.0.thema:16:11
